    {
      "parameters": { "content": "## Idempotency guard\n\"Check Existing Report\" uses `alwaysOutputData: true` so a no-match still produces one item to route on (the zero-item-safety trick). \"Determine Duplicate Status\" then checks whether that item has a real `id` — present only on an actual match — rather than trusting item count.", "height": 200, "width": 860, "color": 4 },
      "id": "1a2085d2-bf0f-43f5-8327-386ba65ad8cf",
      "name": "Sticky Note b35362bf",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [752, 224]
    },
    {
      "parameters": { "content": "## Config-driven setup\nAll per-client values (client name, agency name, sheet ID, threshold, recipient emails, PDF engine choice) live in the Config node at the start of this workflow — that is the only place to edit for a new client. Every node downstream reads from Config via $('Config').item.json.* instead of hardcoding values. Credentials (Sheets/Drive/Gmail/Gemini/PageSpeed) are separate from Config — pick or create each one on its own node.", "height": 440, "width": 300, "color": 6 },
      "id": "98a8d0ec-dbb4-408a-8d4e-2222e5d6a28c",
      "name": "Sticky Note 63e0ceee",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [1872, 272]
    },
    {
      "parameters": { "content": "## Validate-then-stop pattern\nComplex validation logic lives in a Code node (real checks: row presence, numeric types, PageSpeed score present) which sets `isValid` + a human-readable `validationError`. The IF just reads that boolean, keeping the condition itself trivial and the failure message specific. Stop and Error here is what lets CRG - Error Alert catch it with a clear message.", "height": 360, "width": 860, "color": 3 },
      "id": "e9f85616-3ae3-4c6e-bd6d-df89361140a1",
      "name": "Sticky Note 9f1fc335",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [2720, 224]
    },
    {
      "parameters": { "content": "## AI output is untrusted until parsed\nThe Gemini node's response arrives in mergedResponse (confirmed via live testing). This Code node still defensively checks content/text/output/message as a fallback, strips ``` fences, JSON.parse's in a try/catch, and checks the three required keys exist before trusting the result. Malformed AI output fails the run (via Stop and Error) rather than shipping a broken report.", "height": 340, "width": 1140, "color": 3 },
      "id": "0ca90a9a-4c8b-4769-b475-8fc733cdce29",
      "name": "Sticky Note 05d8ca41",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [3552, 384]
    },
    {
      "parameters": { "content": "## Dated folder: always-create (temporary)\nThe Google Drive OAuth credential currently has a restricted scope (drive.file) that blocks the folder *search* call (\"granted scopes do not give access to all of the requested spaces\"). Find-or-create is disabled for now — every run creates a fresh \"Reports - <period>\" folder, so idempotent folder reuse is temporarily off. Reauthorize the Drive credential with full Drive access and reintroduce the search → IF → branch to restore it.", "height": 200, "width": 900 },
      "id": "9f416dda-b237-46c9-ad0a-2f3afa04ce33",
      "name": "Sticky Note 4059396e",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [4400, 544]
    },
    {
      "parameters": { "content": "## Why Upload and Email both branch directly off Render PDF\nGoogle Drive/Gmail action nodes replace $json with their own response and do not reliably pass binary data through. Both nodes read the PDF straight from Render PDF's own output instead of after each other, and pull the report fields (clientName, period, summary) via $('Parse & Validate AI JSON') since that data no longer lives on $json this far downstream.", "height": 440, "width": 580, "color": 5 },
      "id": "9a4a350f-4745-46b1-b65d-2cf75aafb7f6",
      "name": "Sticky Note fea1a329",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [6080, 544]
    }
